  "answer": "To reduce the risk of destructive updates caused by erroneous value estimates, **advantage clipping** has been proposed (https://arxiv.org/abs/2003.06066). The mechanism works by modifying the policy gradient loss to clip negative advantages to zero; this strictly positive clipping prevents policy gradients from reducing the probabilities of sampled actions, thereby suppressing learning from undesired experiences and only reinforcing better-than-expected trajectories (https://arxiv.org/abs/2003.06066)."
